# vim (the host's vi) editing a small file: the alternate screen, the status line,
# insert mode, a scroll, a search, and the shell's screen coming back. Recorded with the
# pinned terminfo entry (TERM as ADR-0333 says) and with Vim's own queries (version and
# cursor position) left in, so that the replayed stream holds queries nothing answers.
# NOTE: `env TERMINFO` is set, but Vim uses its own built-in table for an xterm name (its output has no
# `ESC [ 22 ; 0 ; 0 t`): this recording is of Vim's xterm, not of the pinned entry.
size 80 24
env TERMINFO=@terminfo@
run vi -u NONE -N -n -i NONE --cmd "set nocp ruler showcmd laststatus=2" -c "syntax on" -c "set background=dark" notes.txt
file notes.txt # Notes\nThe quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\nA second line, with a tab:\there.\nTODO: write the terminal.\n\n    indented line\nlast line\n
mark start
send G
wait 1
mark at the last line
send ohello from the editor\e
wait 1
mark after typing
send gg
wait 1
send /fox\r
wait 1
mark after a search
send :set number\r
wait 1
mark with line numbers
send :q!\r
wait 1
mark after quitting
